Frequently Asked Questions

Do I need to create an account?

No. Reflections Looped does not require an account or sign-in.

Where are my lessons and reflections stored?

Your lessons, reflections, and app data are stored locally on your device. Reflections Looped does not use a hosted database to store your personal content.

How do daily lessons work?

Reflections Looped brings previously saved lessons back into your daily feed so you can revisit meaningful insights. You can adjust your daily lesson target in the app.

How do I set up daily reminders?

Open Settings in Reflections Looped and configure your reminder preferences. Allow notifications when prompted. You can also manage notification permissions in your iPhone’s Settings app.

Can I export or back up my data?

Yes. Reflections Looped supports CSV and TXT exports, as well as JSON backups that can be used to restore your saved data.

How do I restore a backup?

Open Settings and select the restore option. Choose a compatible JSON backup file and follow the on-screen instructions. Restoring a backup may replace existing app data, so export anything important first.

How do I delete my data?

Open Settings and select Delete All Data. Confirm the deletion to remove locally stored user data and cancel scheduled reminders.

Previously exported files and backups saved outside the app must be deleted separately.

Can I use Reflections Looped offline?

Yes. The app’s core reflection, lesson, and organization features work without an internet connection.

Is Reflections Looped free?

Yes. Reflections Looped is currently free to use.

Troubleshooting

My daily reminder is not appearing.

Check that reminders are enabled in Reflections Looped and that notifications are allowed under iPhone Settings → Notifications → Reflections Looped.

My saved lessons are missing.

Check your Library and topic filters. If you recently deleted app data or reinstalled the app, you may need to restore a previously saved JSON backup.

I’m having trouble exporting or restoring a file.

Make sure the file is accessible through your iPhone’s Files app. For restoration, use a valid JSON backup created by Reflections Looped.

The app isn’t working as expected.

Try closing and reopening Reflections Looped. If the issue continues, email reflectionslooped@gmail.com with a description of the problem.

